  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Season the chicken with salt, paprika and dried herbs."
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat a large skillet over high and spray with oil then brown the chicken in an even layer, 3-5 minutes."
    },
    {
      "text": "Once browned, remove the chicken, reduce heat and spray with more oil. Add the onion, garlic, ginger, and cook 1 minute, then add the broth to deglaze the pan."
    },
    {
      "text": "Simmer about 1 minute then add in the tomato paste, coconut milk, and 1/2 teaspoon salt."
    },
    {
      "text": "Bring the sauce to a simmer for a few minutes to thicken, add the chicken back along with any juices and cook on medium heat 3 to 4 minutes."
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve over jasmine rice and garnish with cilantro and drizzle with more coconut milk, if desired."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "1. Chicken: Swap chicken breasts with thighs.\n2. Protein: Try with tofu or shrimp, adjusting cooking time as needed.\n3. Vegetarian Coconut Rice Bowls: Omit the chicken, replace the chicken broth with vegetable broth, and add some tofu, and veggies like broccoli, bell pepper, and snap peas.\n4. Curry: Add red curry paste for a coconut curry.\n5. Don’t like cilantro? Skip it or swap it with scallions.\n6. Grains: Serve the coconut chicken over another type of grain, like quinoa or brown rice.",
